    <node id="MAMMOGRAM">
      <data key="d0">MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d1">MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">MAMMOGRAM is an imaging test that produces an x-ray picture of the inside of the breast using low-dose x-rays. It may be performed as a standard 2D digital mammogram or as a 3D mammogram, known as tomosynthesis. The mammogram is used both for breast cancer screening and for the evaluation or diagnosis of breast conditions. It is interpreted by a breast diagnostic radiologist. In addition to screening and diagnosis, a mammogram can also be used to guide a biopsy; when used in this way, the procedure is called a stereotactic needle biopsy.
Relationships:
  - Source: BREAST CANCER SCREENING
  - Target: MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: Mammograms are imaging tests used in breast cancer screening
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: MAMMOGRAM SCREENING
  - Description: Mammogram screening is the use of mammograms to screen for breast cancer
  - Source: MAMMOGRAM
  - Target: SCREENING MAMMOGRAM
  - Description: A mammogram is a medical imaging procedure used to examine breast tissue. A screening mammogram is a specific type of mammogram that is performed regularly as a routine preventive measure, even when the individual has no symptoms or signs of breast disease. Screening mammograms are conducted on a scheduled basis, typically for early detection of breast abnormalities, including cancer, in asymptomatic individuals.</data>
    </node>
