    <node id="INFANT ALL">
      <data key="d0">INFANT ALL</data>
      <data key="d1">INFANT ALL</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Infant ALL is acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) that occurs in infants under 12 months of age. Its treatment approach is distinct from that used for other age groups, reflecting the unique biological and clinical features of the disease in this very young population.
Relationships:
  - Source: ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA
  - Target: INFANT ALL
  - Description: Infant ALL is ALL in infants under 12 months of age.
  - Source: NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK
  - Target: INFANT ALL
  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides clinical guidance through its NCCN Guidelines, which include dedicated content addressing infant acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL). Specifically, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients contain a chapter that discusses infant ALL, and the broader NCCN Guidelines also include a chapter focused on infant ALL treatment. These materials are part of the organization’s efforts to offer evidence-based recommendations and patient-oriented information for this rare and challenging form of leukemia.
  - Source: ALL
  - Target: INFANT ALL
  - Description: Infant ALL is ALL occurring in children under 12 months of age.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
