Relationships:
  - Source: NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK
  - Target: INFANT ALL
  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides clinical guidance through its NCCN Guidelines, which include dedicated content addressing infant acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL). Specifically, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients contain a chapter that discusses infant ALL, and the broader NCCN Guidelines also include a chapter focused on infant ALL treatment. These materials are part of the organization’s efforts to offer evidence-based recommendations and patient-oriented information for this rare and challenging form of leukemia.</data>
