    <node id="QUITTING SMOKING">
      <data key="d0">QUITTING SMOKING</data>
      <data key="d1">QUITTING SMOKING</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Quitting smoking is the process of stopping the use of tobacco cigarettes and other smoked products. It is a significant health intervention that may reduce cancer risk and improve outcomes for cancer treatment, particularly for bladder cancer. The act of quitting smoking is supported by a range of resources, including counseling, medications, and online tools, all of which can help individuals succeed in their efforts. By discontinuing smoking, individuals can experience better cancer treatment results and lower their overall risk of developing cancer. This comprehensive approach highlights both the health benefits and the practical support available for those seeking to quit.
Relationships:
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: SMOKING
  - Description: Quitting smoking is the act of stopping smoking
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: CANCER TREATMENT
  - Description: Quitting smoking can make cancer treatment work better
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: NICOTINE WITHDRAWAL
  - Description: Nicotine withdrawal is challenging for people who smoke and try to quit
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: BLADDER CANCER
  - Description: Quitting smoking may help bladder cancer treatments work better
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Description: Quitting smoking can lead to better cancer treatment outcomes
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: CANCER
  - Description: Quitting smoking can lead to better cancer treatment outcomes
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support resource to help people quit smoking
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Description: BeTobaccoFree.gov is listed as an online support resource to help people quit smoking
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: CDC.gov/tobacco is listed as an online support resource to help people quit smoking
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The care team can provide counseling and medicines to help a patient quit smoking or vaping
  - Source: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Target: SMOKING
  - Description: The text advises people who smoke to seek help to quit</data>
