    <node id="DOCTOR">
      <data key="d0">DOCTOR</data>
      <data key="d1">DOCTOR</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">The doctor is a physician and healthcare professional who serves as a key member of the patient's care team. In this role, they conduct comprehensive assessments, including asking about symptoms, performing physical exams (such as skin exams, lymph node examinations, and digital rectal exams), and reviewing the patient’s family health history of blood relatives to help determine the best treatment approach. The doctor evaluates the patient’s cancer risk, reviews prior surgery and biopsy results, and guides treatment decisions. They also review pathology reports with the patient, may suggest genetic testing, and can refer the patient to a genetic counselor.

The doctor is responsible for discussing test results—including imaging, laboratory, and blood or biochemical tests—with the patient, receiving and interpreting these results, and ordering additional tests as needed. They may order imaging tests during follow-up after cancer treatment. In addition, the doctor selects the biopsy method, discusses biopsy risks and scarring, and may order imaging tests. For confirmed squamous cell skin cancer, the doctor evaluates features to determine whether the cancer is low-, high-, or very high-risk and considers appropriate treatment options.

Beyond diagnosis and treatment planning, the doctor addresses broader patient concerns. They are consulted about birth control options, pregnancy planning, and other treatment-related concerns, and they may prescribe treatments such as iron supplements. The doctor also explains medical information clearly; patients are encouraged to ask for simpler terms when needed. Throughout the care journey, the doctor is a central contact with whom the patient discusses test results and attends visits, ensuring continuity of care and coordination of next steps.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: PATIENT
  - Target: DOCTOR
  - Description: The patient and the doctor are engaged in an ongoing medical consultation. During their visits, the patient actively asks questions and discusses test results with the doctor. The patient also seeks guidance on birth control options and consults the doctor about the best time to plan a pregnancy. Through these interactions, the patient works with the doctor to address reproductive health concerns and make informed decisions.
  - Source: DOCTOR
  - Target: PATIENT
  - Description: Dr. [Doctor] provides ongoing care for the patient, including performing skin exams as part of their medical treatment. The patient, in turn, actively participates in their care by asking the doctor to review their pathology report. Together, these interactions reflect a collaborative doctor-patient relationship focused on evaluation, diagnosis, and informed treatment decisions.

---

