  - Description: The care team conducts doctor visits and appointments

  - Source: PATIENT
  - Target: DOCTOR VISITS
  - Description: Patients attend doctor visits and are encouraged to bring someone for support

---</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APPOINTMENTS">
      <data key="d0">APPOINTMENTS</data>
      <data key="d1">APPOINTMENTS</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">APPOINTMENTS are scheduled clinical visits during which a patient meets with their care team to ask questions and discuss care. These interactions may take place in person as doctor visits or remotely as telehealth visits. Patients are encouraged to prepare for appointments by bringing someone for support and taking notes. Tracking appointments through a patient portal such as MyChart is recommended, as the portal helps patients keep track of scheduled visits and communicate with the care team. Overall, appointments are medical visits or meetings that patients should track and prepare for to ensure productive discussions about their care.
**Relationships:** None listed in the provided data.

---</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EYE EXAM">
      <data key="d0">EYE EXAM</data>
      <data key="d1">EYE EXAM</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">An eye exam is a medical test used to evaluate the health of the eyes, particularly the nerves at the back of the eyes, and it may be performed as part of a broader neurological examination. The exam serves multiple diagnostic and precautionary purposes. It is used to detect the presence of primary CNS lymphoma, a type of cancer that can occur in the eyes. Additionally, an eye exam may be recommended before starting treatment for nasopharyngeal cancer, because this cancer can also affect the eyes. By assessing the condition of the ocular nerves and overall eye health, the eye exam helps in the early detection of these conditions and in guiding treatment decisions.
Relationships:
  - Source: EYE EXAM
  - Target: PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA
  - Description: An eye exam is performed because primary CNS lymphoma can affect the eyes

  - Source: NEUROLOGICAL EXAM
  - Target: EYE EXAM
  - Description: An eye exam may be performed as part of the neurological exam to check optic-nerve health.

  - Source: DIAGNOSIS
  - Target: EYE EXAM
  - Description: Eye exam helps diagnose primary CNS lymphoma if the eyes are involved

  - Source: PATIENT
  - Target: EYE EXAM
  - Description: An eye exam might be recommended for the patient before starting treatment

---</data>
