    <node id="HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT">
      <data key="d0">HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT</data>
      <data key="d1">HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT is a medical treatment that replaces the patient's blood-forming stem cells. It is used as a therapeutic approach for acute myeloid leukemia (AML), serving as a treatment type specifically aimed at restoring healthy blood cell production by substituting the patient's compromised stem cells with new, healthy ones. This concise definition encompasses the procedure's core function as a stem cell replacement therapy and its application in the context of AML treatment.
Relationships:
