    <node id="PET">
      <data key="d0">PET</data>
      <data key="d1">PET</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">PET (Positron Emission Tomography) is an imaging test used in the initial evaluation of cervical cancer. It may be performed as part of the initial imaging workup for individuals diagnosed with cervical cancer. The primary purpose of PET in this setting is to determine the extent of the disease before treatment begins, helping to establish how far the cancer has spread. By providing this information, PET assists clinicians in staging cervical cancer and planning appropriate treatment.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
