    <node id="PALLIATIVE RADIATION THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">PALLIATIVE RADIATION THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d1">PALLIATIVE RADIATION THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Palliative radiation therapy is a form of treatment used to limit tumor size and alleviate symptoms when cancer is causing distress. Its primary goal is not to cure the cancer, but to improve the patient's quality of life by reducing pain, pressure, or other symptoms resulting from the tumor. This approach carefully avoids re-treating previously irradiated areas, thereby minimizing additional harm and respecting prior radiation exposure.
**Relationships:** None listed in the provided data.

---</data>
