    <node id="PHASE 2 TRIALS">
      <data key="d0">PHASE 2 TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d1">PHASE 2 TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Phase 2 trials, also known as Phase 2 clinical trials, are a phase of clinical research that focuses on evaluating how well a drug or treatment approach works against a specific type of cancer. These trials are designed to assess the effectiveness of the intervention in a particular patient population, providing critical data on whether the treatment produces the desired effect. In summary, Phase 2 trials are clinical trials that study the efficacy of a drug or therapeutic approach against a defined cancer type.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: PHASE 2 TRIALS
  - Description: Phase 2 trials are a phase of clinical trials studying effectiveness against a specific type of cancer.

---</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: PHASE 2 TRIALS
Description: Phase 2 trials, also known as Phase 2 clinical trials, are a phase of clinical research that focuses on evaluating how well a drug or treatment approach works against a specific type of cancer. These trials are designed to assess the effectiveness of the intervention in a particular patient population, providing critical data on whether the treatment produces the desired effect. In summary, Phase 2 trials are clinical trials that study the efficacy of a drug or therapeutic approach against a defined cancer type.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: PHASE 2 TRIALS
  - Description: Phase 2 trials are a phase of clinical trials studying effectiveness against a specific type of cancer.

