    <node id="TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)">
      <data key="d0">TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)</data>
      <data key="d1">TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">TURBT is a procedure that examines tumors on the bladder wall and removes them, used as a treatment option for bladder cancer.
Relationships:
  - Source: TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)
  - Target: RADICAL CYSTECTOMY
  - Description: Both TURBT and radical cystectomy are surgical treatment options for bladder cancer; TURBT removes tumors from the bladder wall and radical cystectomy removes the bladder.
  - Source: TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)
  - Target: BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY
