    <node id="LAB">
      <data key="d0">LAB</data>
      <data key="d1">LAB</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">LAB is a specialized medical facility that receives biological samples—including biopsy samples (such as skin biopsies), blood, and urine—for diagnostic testing. These samples are sent to the lab for microscopic examination and analysis of cells, proteins, and other components. The primary purpose of the lab is to detect disease or other medical conditions. In particular, it is where a pathologist examines and tests biopsy samples to identify cancer and other abnormalities. In essence, LAB functions as a central diagnostic site where biopsy samples are sent for testing and where laboratory professionals and pathologists analyze specimens to support patient diagnosis and treatment.
Relationships: (None listed in the provided data)</data>
    </node>
