    <node id="COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL">
      <data key="d0">COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL</data>
      <data key="d1">COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">The Comprehensive Metabolic Panel (CMP) is a blood test that measures a variety of substances in the blood to provide detailed information about kidney and liver function. It serves as a screening tool for up to 14 different chemicals, helping to assess overall metabolic health. In particular, the CMP evaluates markers related to kidney function, liver function, and includes measurements such as calcium levels. By analyzing these substances, the test aids in detecting, diagnosing, or monitoring conditions affecting the kidneys and liver, as well as broader metabolic imbalances.
Relationships:
  - Source: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
  - Target: CREATININE
  - Description: CMP measures creatinine to assess kidney function
  - Source: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
  - Target: BLOOD UREA NITROGEN
  - Description: CMP measures BUN to assess kidney function
  - Source: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
  - Target: BLOOD TESTS
  - Description: A comprehensive metabolic panel is a type of blood test described in the text.
  - Source: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The care team uses CMP to check kidney and liver function
  - Source: CLL
  - Target: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
  - Description: Comprehensive metabolic panel is a test used to plan CLL treatment.
  - Source: COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL
  - Target: ELECTROLYTES
  - Description: CMP measures electrolytes to assess body function</data>
    </node>
