    <node id="BRAIN MRI SCAN">
      <data key="d0">BRAIN MRI SCAN</data>
      <data key="d1">BRAIN MRI SCAN</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A brain MRI scan is a diagnostic imaging procedure used to examine the brain, specifically to detect swelling of the outer layer of the brain, a condition known as leukemic meningitis, which can arise from leukemia. This scan utilizes radio waves and powerful magnets to create detailed images, and it does not use x-rays. The procedure is also described as an MRI scan of the brain that can reveal this leukemia-related swelling of the brain's outer layer.
Relationships:
  - Source: MRI SCAN
  - Target: BRAIN MRI SCAN
  - Description: A brain MRI scan is an MRI scan of the brain
  - Source: BRAIN MRI SCAN
  - Target: MRI (MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING) SCAN
  - Description: A brain MRI scan is an MRI scan focused on the brain</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
