      <data key="d1">CLOSED MRI</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A closed MRI is a type of MRI machine characterized by a capsule-like, enclosed design in which the magnet surrounds the patient. The space inside is small and fully enclosed, which can contribute to feelings of claustrophobia for some patients. Closed MRI scanners are more common than open MRI machines and are widely used for diagnostic imaging.
