    <node id="OPEN MRI">
      <data key="d0">OPEN MRI</data>
      <data key="d1">OPEN MRI</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">OPEN MRI is a type of MRI machine that features a magnetic top and bottom, leaving openings on each end. This design makes the scanner less confining and is especially useful for patients who experience claustrophobia, as the open sides help reduce the feeling of being enclosed. Compared to traditional closed MRI scanners, open MRI machines are less commonly used; closed MRIs remain the more prevalent option in medical imaging.
