    <node id="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d1">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Platinum chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment that uses drugs containing the metal platinum. This category includes well-known agents such as cisplatin and carboplatin. It is commonly administered during radiation therapy, often concurrently with external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) as part of a chemoradiation regimen. This approach is specifically utilized in the treatment of cancers such as squamous cell skin cancer and cervical cancer, among others. As a systemic therapy, platinum chemotherapy works by interfering with DNA replication in rapidly dividing cancer cells, enhancing the effects of radiation when given together.
Relationships: (none listed in the provided data)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
