    <node id="FOLFOX">
      <data key="d0">FOLFOX</data>
      <data key="d1">FOLFOX</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">FOLFOX is a chemotherapy regimen that combines three drugs: 5-fluorouracil (5-FU), leucovorin, and oxaliplatin. It is specifically recommended for the treatment of high-risk stage 2 and stage 3 colon cancers. The standard course of FOLFOX therapy is administered over a period of 6 months. This regimen is a common and effective option in adjuvant chemotherapy for these colon cancer stages, aiming to reduce the risk of recurrence after surgery.
Relationships: (none listed in the provided data)</data>
