    <node id="HYSTERECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">HYSTERECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d1">HYSTERECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of the uterus, which permanently eliminates the possibility of carrying a pregnancy. In the context of cervical cancer, this surgery typically includes removal of the cervix as well as the uterus, making it a treatment option for the disease. However, hysterectomy is only considered an appropriate treatment for cervical cancer when the cancer has not spread beyond the cervix; it is not performed if the cancer has metastasized to other areas.
**Relationships:** (No direct relationships listed in the data)</data>
