      <data key="d1">FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Follow-up and surveillance is the process of testing after cancer treatment to find early signs that the cancer may have returned.
Relationships:
  - Source: NCCN
  - Target: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Description: NCCN provides patient information and guidelines that include follow-up and surveillance recommendations.
  - Source: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: IMAGING TESTS
  - Description: During follow-up and surveillance, the doctor may order imaging tests.
  - Source: CHEMORADIATION
  - Target: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Description: Follow-up and surveillance begins after treatment with chemoradiation is completed.
  - Source: DOCTOR
  - Target: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Description: The doctor participates in follow-up and surveillance by ordering tests and evaluating the results.
  - Source: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: PHYSICAL EXAM
  - Description: Follow-up and surveillance includes a physical exam with digital rectal examination and anoscopy.
  - Source: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: ANOSCOPY
  - Description: Follow-up and surveillance includes anoscopy.
  - Source: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: COMPLETE REMISSION
  - Description: Surveillance results determine whether the cancer is in complete remission.
  - Source: FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE
  - Target: DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION
  - Description: Follow-up and surveillance includes digital rectal examination.</data>
