    <node id="HEPATITIS B">
      <data key="d0">HEPATITIS B</data>
      <data key="d1">HEPATITIS B</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Hepatitis B is a viral infection caused by the hepatitis B virus (HBV). It is clinically significant in multiple contexts, including as a required screening test before treatment for chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL), due to the risk of viral reactivation during immunosuppressive therapy. The infection can lead to serious liver-related complications, including chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer. Additionally, the presence of chronic hepatitis B is an established indication for regular liver cancer screening, as it substantially increases the risk of hepatocellular carcinoma.
Relationships:
  - Source: HEPATITIS B
  - Target: LIVER CANCER
  - Description: Hepatitis B is a risk factor for liver cancer.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS B
  - Description: Hepatitis B virus or infection can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: HEPATITIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS B
  - Description: Hepatitis B is one of the viruses that cause hepatitis.
  - Source: HEPATITIS B
