      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Follow-up testing is the regular surveillance process conducted after bladder cancer treatment to monitor for potential recurrence. Its primary purpose is to check whether the cancer has returned and to detect any new cancer growth at the earliest possible stage, allowing for timely intervention if needed.
