    <node id="HEALTH CHECKUP (REPEATED FOR COMPLETENESS)">
      <data key="d0">HEALTH CHECKUP (REPEATED FOR COMPLETENESS)</data>
      <data key="d1">HEALTH CHECKUP (REPEATED FOR COMPLETENESS)</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">HEALTH CHECKUP is a medical examination performed to evaluate a patient’s health status. In the context of post-treatment care, it is used to assess a patient’s recovery, blood counts, and overall condition after stem cell rescue treatment. Additionally, a health checkup may refer to a regular medical visit during which preventive services such as breast cancer screening and consultations with health care providers can take place. These two roles are complementary, reflecting both focused follow-up after a specific procedure and routine preventive care.  
**Relationships:**  
  - Source: BREAST CANCER  
  - Target: HEALTH CHECKUP  
  - Description: Health checkups can include breast cancer screening and discussion of breast health  
  - Source: HEALTH CHECKUP  
  - Target: STEM CELL RESCUE  
  - Description: Health checkups are recommended after stem cell rescue to monitor recovery.  
  - Source: HEALTH CHECKUP  
  - Target: BLOOD TEST  
  - Description: Blood tests and health checkups are both part of post-stem-cell-rescue monitoring.  
  - Source: BREAST CANCER SCREENING  
  - Target: HEALTH CHECKUP  
  - Description: Regular health checkups are opportunities for breast cancer screening  

