    <node id="LYMPHOMA">
      <data key="d0">LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d1">LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Lymphoma is a cancer of lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell that plays a central role in the immune system. It is characterized by an abnormal overgrowth of these cells, which can accumulate in lymph nodes and other tissues. One specific form is primary CNS lymphoma, which arises in the central nervous system. In the context of treatment described here, high-dose chemotherapy is administered to kill lymphoma cells throughout the body during a procedure known as a stem cell rescue, which helps restore healthy blood-forming cells after the intensive therapy.
Relationships: (None listed in the data)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: LYMPHOMA
Description: Lymphoma is a cancer of lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell that plays a central role in the immune system. It is characterized by an abnormal overgrowth of these cells, which can accumulate in lymph nodes and other tissues. One specific form is primary CNS lymphoma, which arises in the central nervous system. In the context of treatment described here, high-dose chemotherapy is administered to kill lymphoma cells throughout the body during a procedure known as a stem cell rescue, which helps restore healthy blood-forming cells after the intensive therapy.
Relationships: (None listed in the data)</data>
    </node>
