      <data key="d0">MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d1">MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST is a physician who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of cancer through the use of systemic drug therapy. As a key member of the cancer care team, a medical oncologist treats cancer using medications that may be administered by mouth, injection, or intravenously. This specialist is specifically trained to prescribe and manage cancer-treatment drugs, including chemotherapy, and plays a central role in coordinating a patient's overall cancer treatment plan.
Relationships: (None listed in the data)</data>
