    <node id="WBRT">
      <data key="d0">WBRT</data>
      <data key="d1">WBRT</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">WBRT (whole brain radiation therapy) is a radiation therapy technique used to treat primary CNS lymphoma by radiating the whole brain. It can be expanded to include the eyes or replaced by focused eye radiation, and may cause vision problems, cataracts, memory problems, slowed thinking, and trouble speaking.
Relationships:
  - Source: WBRT
  - Target: RADIATION THERAPY FOR THE EYES
  - Description: WBRT can be expanded to include the eyes, or eye-only radiation can be used instead

  - Source: WBRT
  - Target: PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA IN THE EYES
  - Description: WBRT can be expanded to include the eyes for primary CNS lymphoma in the eyes

---</data>
    </node>
