      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT is a bone imaging test used to evaluate skeletal conditions. It may not be necessary in cases where an FDG-PET/CT scan has already clearly demonstrated the presence of cancer in the bone. In such instances, the additional sodium fluoride PET/CT provides redundant information and can be avoided.  
**Relationships:** (None directly listed in the provided data)  

