      <data key="d6">: ENDORECTAL ULTRASOUND is recommended during surveillance after ESD and transanal local excision, and it is an alternative to pelvic MRI with contrast [Data: Relationships (2893, 2895, 2896); Entities (1124, 1144)]. This connects it to ongoing assessment of recurrence, which is tied to staging and treatment decisions.
</data>
    </node>
