      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY (CT) SCAN is an imaging test that combines a computer with an X-ray machine to produce detailed, three-dimensional pictures of tissues and organs inside the body. In the context of cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC), a CT scan is specifically recommended to evaluate lymph nodes near the affected area after a biopsy has confirmed regional spread of the disease. Thus, it serves both as a general diagnostic imaging tool and as a targeted method for assessing lymph node involvement in CSCC cases.
Relationships:
  - (No explicit relationships listed in the provided data)</data>
