      <data key="d3">Lymph node removal is a surgical procedure in which one or more lymph nodes are excised for examination during pathologic staging. It involves the surgical removal of lymph nodes, including pelvic and para-aortic nodes, to help limit the spread of cancer cells and determine the extent of cancer.
Relationships:
