    <edge source="CDC" target="CDC.GOV/TOBACCO" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CDC</data>
      <data key="d8">CDC.GOV/TOBACCO</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) operates the online resource CDC.gov/tobacco, which serves as the agency's dedicated digital platform for tobacco cessation. As the CDC's official online tobacco cessation resource, CDC.gov/tobacco provides information and support to help individuals quit tobacco use, reflecting the CDC's broader public health mission to reduce tobacco-related disease and death. This platform is a key component of the CDC's efforts to offer accessible cessation guidance and resources to the public.</data>
      <data key="d12">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CDC" target="CANCER TREATMENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CDC</data>
      <data key="d8">CANCER TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">CDC.gov/tobacco provides smoking cessation resources; quitting smoking/vaping is important for effective cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CDC" target="SMOKEFREE.GOV" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CDC</data>
      <data key="d8">SMOKEFREE.GOV</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">SmokeFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support option to help people quit smoking or vaping, while the CDCs website, CDC.gov/tobacco, is also listed as an online support resource for quitting tobacco. Together, they serve as accessible digital tools for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and assistance to those looking to stop using tobacco products.</data>
      <data key="d12">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CDC" target="BETOBACCOFREE.GOV" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CDC</data>
      <data key="d8">BETOBACCOFREE.GOV</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">BeTobaccoFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, the CDC provides these resources through its dedicated website, CDC.gov/tobacco. Together, BeTobaccoFree.gov and the CDC serve as accessible online support options to help people quit smoking or vaping. Both entities are listed as credible sources of assistance for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and resources for those looking to stop using tobacco products.</data>
      <data key="d12">CDC</data>
    </edge>
