      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">SUPPORTIVE CARE</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Supportive care is a type of treatment and care option, particularly used for acute myeloid leukemia (AML). Its primary purpose is to help manage the side effects of the disease and its treatment, aiming to improve the patient's quality of life and overall well-being. As a form of treatment, supportive care works alongside other medical interventions to address complications, reduce symptoms, and support the patient throughout their care journey.</data>
      <data key="d12">SUPPORTIVE CARE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TREATMENT" target="CLINICAL TRIALS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Clinical trials are a type of treatment option, specifically one that may be recommended for patients with acute myeloid leukemia (AML). As a treatment approach, clinical trials offer eligible individuals access to investigational therapies and contribute to the advancement of medical knowledge.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TREATMENT" target="SIDE EFFECTS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">SIDE EFFECTS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Treatments can cause side effects and side effects are a key part of treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d12">SIDE EFFECTS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TREATMENT" target="RADIATION THERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">RADIATION THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Radiation therapy is a type of treatment that falls under the broader category of medical treatments. Specifically, it is a type of cancer treatment, used to address malignant diseases. Additionally, radiation therapy is a type of treatment for cervical cancer, indicating its application in managing that particular form of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADIATION THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TREATMENT" target="TARGETED THERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">TARGETED THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Targeted therapy is a form of cancer treatment that specifically targets the molecular mechanisms driving cancer growth. It is also a recognized type of treatment for acute myeloid leukemia (AML), commonly described as a type of AML treatment or a treatment option for AML. In the context of AML, targeted therapy works by interfering with specific genetic mutations, proteins, or pathways that contribute to the development and survival of leukemic cells, thereby distinguishing it from traditional chemotherapy. Thus, both as a general cancer treatment and as a specific AML treatment, targeted therapy plays a critical role in offering more precise, often less toxic, therapeutic choices for patients.</data>
      <data key="d12">TARGETED THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TREATMENT" target="HISTOLOGY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">HISTOLOGY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Histology is used to make treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d12">HISTOLOGY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TREATMENT" target="CHEMOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d8">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Chemotherapy is a form of medical treatment used primarily in oncology. As a cancer treatment, chemotherapy involves the use of cytotoxic drugs to destroy or inhibit the growth of cancer cells. It is applicable across multiple cancer types and is often integrated into broader therapeutic protocols. Specifically, chemotherapy is a recognized type of treatment for acute myeloid leukemia (AML), where it serves as the standard-of-care approach for managing this blood cancer. In addition to its role in AML, chemotherapy is also a component of cervical cancer treatment, frequently administered as part of chemoradiationa combination of chemotherapy and radiation therapy that enhances the effectiveness of treatment. As such, chemotherapy occupies a central position within the overall category of cancer treatment, functioning both as a standalone modality and as an adjunct to other therapies. The entity TREATMENT encompasses a wide range of medical interventions, and chemotherapy is one of its key subtypes, distinguished by its mechanism of action and its established role in hematologic and solid tumor malignancies. Overall, chemotherapy exemplifies a targeted and evidence-based treatment option, with particular significance in AML, where it is the established standard of care, and in cervical cancer, where it is integrated into combined-modality regimens.</data>
      <data key="d12">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
