      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">CT scan is an imaging test, one of the imaging tests described in the provided text. As a diagnostic tool, it is used to detect the spread of cancer to the chest and abdomen. Additionally, CT scan is used to look for ovarian cancer and its spread. In the context of prostate cancer, imaging methods include CT, meaning that CT scan is also utilized for prostate cancer evaluation. Thus, CT scan serves as a versatile imaging modality across multiple cancer types, including ovarian and prostate cancers, as well as for assessing metastasis to the chest and abdomen.</data>
