    <edge source="LUMBAR PUNCTURE" target="SPINAL TAP" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">LUMBAR PUNCTURE</data>
      <data key="d8">SPINAL TAP</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A lumbar puncture, also known as a spinal tap, is a medical procedure. Both nameslumbar puncture and spinal taprefer to the same diagnostic and therapeutic technique. The procedure involves inserting a needle into the lower back to access the subarachnoid space in order to collect cerebrospinal fluid for analysis, measure pressure, or administer medication. It is performed by a trained healthcare professional and is commonly used to help diagnose conditions affecting the central nervous system, such as infections, inflammation, or bleeding.</data>
      <data key="d12">LUMBAR PUNCTURE</data>
    </edge>
