    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="CLINICAL TRIALS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Systemic therapy and clinical trials are both treatment options for squamous cell skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIALS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Enrolling in a clinical trial for systemic therapy is an option.</data>
      <data key="d12">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="TARGETED THERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">TARGETED THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Targeted therapy is a type of systemic therapy, meaning it is a systemic treatment that travels throughout the body to reach cancer cells. However, unlike broader systemic treatments, targeted therapy specifically attacks cancer cells by focusing on specific molecules or pathways involved in tumor growth and survival. While both SYSTEMIC THERAPY and TARGETED THERAPY are related, targeted therapy is categorized under the broader umbrella of systemic therapy, which encompasses treatments that affect the whole body rather than a localized area. Thus, TARGETED THERAPY is a specialized form of SYSTEMIC THERAPY that aims to precisely target cancer cells while distinguishing them from normal cells.</data>
      <data key="d12">TARGETED THERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYSTEMIC THERAPY" target="PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SYSTEMIC THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Systemic therapy is a treatment approach used in cancer care, encompassing a range of drug-based treatments that circulate throughout the body. When systemic therapy is planned, platinum-based chemotherapy is a recommended option. This is particularly relevant in the context of metastatic cervical cancer, where systemic therapy is usually platinum-based chemotherapy. Thus, platinum-based chemotherapy serves as a key component of systemic therapy, especially for patients with metastatic cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d12">PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EBRT" target="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">EBRT</data>
      <data key="d8">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">EBRT is given together with platinum chemotherapy as part of chemoradiation for cervical cancer</data>
      <data key="d12">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIATION THERAPY" target="CERVICAL CANCER" id="related_to">
