    <edge source="NCCN FOUNDATION" target="UNITED STATES" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN FOUNDATION</data>
      <data key="d8">UNITED STATES</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The NCCN Foundation funds the nation's promising doctors at the center of innovation in cancer research.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN FOUNDATION" target="PFIZER INC." id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NCCN FOUNDATION</data>
      <data key="d8">PFIZER INC.</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Pfizer Inc. is a corporate supporter acknowledged by the NCCN Foundation for helping to make available the NCCN Guidelines for Patients. Pfizer Inc. is a corporate supporter acknowledged by the NCCN Foundation for helping make the NCCN Guidelines for Patients available.</data>
      <data key="d12">PFIZER INC.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="NCCN CANCER CENTERS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The NCCN Cancer Centers serve as a key resource for locating clinical trials, specifically within the United States. These centers assist patients in identifying and accessing clinical trial opportunities, making them a valuable source of information for those seeking participation in research studies. The entity CLINICAL TRIAL is central to this resource, as the primary function of the NCCN Cancer Centers is to connect individuals with relevant clinical trials. In summary, NCCN Cancer Centers provide a United Statesbased resource dedicated to helping patients find clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN CANCER CENTERS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="INFORMED CONSENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">INFORMED CONSENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A clinical trial is a research study conducted with human participants to evaluate medical, surgical, or behavioral interventions. As part of the clinical trial enrollment process, researchers provide an informed consent form to potential participants before enrollment. This informed consent document explains the study's purpose, the potential risks involved, and the anticipated benefits. By reviewing and signing the informed consent form, participants acknowledge that they understand what the clinical trial entails and voluntarily agree to take part. Both the clinical trial process and the informed consent mechanism work together to ensure that participants are fully educated about the study before making a decision to enroll. The descriptions emphasize that informed consent is a critical and integral component of clinical trial enrollment, serving as a formal communication tool that outlines essential study information in an accessible manner.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="NCCN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">NCCN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCCN Cancer Centers and NCCN patient guidelines provide information about cancer clinical trials and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">NCCN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="SURGERY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">SURGERY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Enrolling in a clinical trial is another treatment option alongside surgery for eligible patients.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="CARE TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team plays a key role in evaluating whether a clinical trial is appropriate for a patient. They can be consulted directly to determine if a clinical trial might be right for the individual. To make this determination, the care team uses the patient's performance status as a key factor in assessing eligibility for a clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="TREATMENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">TREATMENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A clinical trial is a treatment option that may be considered for a patient. Clinical trials offer potential new therapies and serve as another treatment option.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="UNITED STATES" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">UNITED STATES</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The text describes finding clinical trials in the United States.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NCI provides a portal for patients to search for cancer clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">NLM maintains clinicaltrials.gov, where patients can search for clinical trials worldwide.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="PHASE 3 TRIALS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">PHASE 3 TRIALS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Phase 3 trials are a phase of clinical trials comparing a new approach to a standard treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="PHASE 2 TRIALS" id="related_to">
