    </edge>
    <edge source="CLINICAL TRIAL" target="PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d8">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Joining a clinical trial is a recommended option for treating primary CNS lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d12">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The U.S. National Library of Medicine maintains ClinicalTrials.gov, a comprehensive worldwide clinical trial registry and search database. This resource is provided by the U.S. National Library of Medicine to help users find clinical trials. ClinicalTrials.gov serves as a global repository, allowing researchers, patients, and the public to locate and access information about clinical trials conducted around the world.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE" target="UNITED STATES" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE</data>
      <data key="d8">UNITED STATES</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) is a U.S. federal institution and government organization operating within the United States. As a U.S. government library, it is explicitly identified as an American institution and serves as the national library of medicine for the country. In addition to its role as a federal library, the NLM is known for providing the ClinicalTrials.gov database, a key resource for clinical research information. The NLM operates under the broader framework of the United States, functioning as a U.S. government entity dedicated to medical and health information.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMOR HPV TESTING" target="HPV-RELATED CANCER" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TUMOR HPV TESTING</data>
      <data key="d8">HPV-RELATED CANCER</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Tumor HPV testing can identify whether a cancer is HPV-related.</data>
      <data key="d12">HPV-RELATED CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMOR HPV TESTING" target="BIOPSY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TUMOR HPV TESTING</data>
      <data key="d8">BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A tumor or blood sample is tested for HPV DNA in tumor HPV testing.</data>
      <data key="d12">TUMOR HPV TESTING</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Cancer Institute (NCI) provides comprehensive clinical trial information and search resources. These resources are available through the NCI's official website at cancer.gov/about-cancer/treatment/clinical-trials/search, where patients, caregivers, and researchers can locate ongoing clinical trials. In addition to the online search tool, the National Cancer Institute's Cancer Information Service is also available to help individuals find clinical trials that may be relevant to their needs. Together, these offerings ensure that the public has access to both self-service search tools and personalized assistance when seeking information about clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE" target="UNITED STATES" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE</data>
      <data key="d8">UNITED STATES</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. government organization operating within the United States. It is formally a U.S. government agency and institute, and it is located in the United States. The NCI is also listed under "In the United States" as a resource for finding clinical trials, reflecting its role in providing access to cancer research and treatment information. As a government entity, the NCI operates as part of the U.S. federal structure, dedicated to cancer research and related public health efforts.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
