    <edge source="STEM CELL RESCUE" target="PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">STEM CELL RESCUE</data>
      <data key="d8">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Stem cell rescue may be used for primary CNS lymphoma after other treatments or relapse</data>
      <data key="d12">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STEM CELL RESCUE" target="RELAPSE" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">STEM CELL RESCUE</data>
      <data key="d8">RELAPSE</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Stem cell rescue is a treatment approach used for lymphoma when the disease has returned after an initial course of therapy. Specifically, it is indicated in the context of a relapse, meaning the lymphoma has come back following earlier treatment. The procedure is employed after the relapse occurs, serving as a subsequent line of intervention. Thus, stem cell rescue is directly associated with managing recurrent lymphoma, with the goal of addressing the disease after prior treatment has failed to provide a lasting remission.</data>
      <data key="d12">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
    </edge>
