      <data key="d12">U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Cancer Information Service assists individuals in locating appropriate clinical trials, including providing guidance on how to find them. It also answers cancer-related questions and addresses specific inquiries about clinical trials, such as their purpose, procedures, and eligibility. Additionally, the service offers contact information for further assistance, ensuring that individuals have access to the support they need when seeking information about cancer and clinical trial participation.</data>
      <data key="d12">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE" target="UNITED STATES" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE</data>
      <data key="d8">UNITED STATES</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Cancer Information Service is a U.S.-based entity that operates as part of the National Cancer Institute, which is also based in the United States. As a service of this institute, it is situated within the broader organizational framework of the U.S. National Cancer Institute, reflecting its role in providing cancer-related information and support within the United States.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
