    <edge source="SCREENING MAMMOGRAM" target="DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">SCREENING MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d8">DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">A screening mammogram is an initial imaging exam used to detect potential breast abnormalities in individuals without symptoms. When a screening mammogram reveals an abnormal area, a diagnostic mammogram is performed as a follow-up. A diagnostic mammogram is used to take a closer look at the abnormal area found on the screening mammogram, providing more detailed images to help determine whether the finding is benign or requires further investigation. Together, the screening mammogram serves as the first-line detection tool, while the diagnostic mammogram provides focused evaluation of any suspicious findings identified during screening.</data>
      <data key="d12">SCREENING MAMMOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
