    <edge source="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY" target="CHEMORADIATION" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">CHEMORADIATION</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Chemoradiation is a cancer treatment modality that combines radiation therapy with platinum chemotherapy. Specifically, chemoradiation consists of external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) delivered alongside platinum-based chemotherapy agents. This approach integrates the radiosensitizing and cytotoxic effects of platinum chemotherapy with the targeted tumor-killing effects of EBRT, allowing for enhanced treatment efficacy. In this context, the platinum chemotherapy is administered concurrently with radiation, and this combination is referred to as chemoradiation. Thus, the entity known as PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY is a key component of CHEMORADIATION, which is defined by the pairing of platinum drugs with external beam radiation.</data>
      <data key="d12">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY" target="BRACHYTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">BRACHYTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Brachytherapy may be given along with platinum chemotherapy in the treatment of locally advanced cervical cancer</data>
      <data key="d12">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY" target="VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY" id="related_to">
