    <edge source="MENSTRUAL CYCLE" target="PREGNANCY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MENSTRUAL CYCLE</data>
      <data key="d8">PREGNANCY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The menstrual cycle and pregnancy are interrelated biological processes in which the hormone progesterone plays a key role. The menstrual cycle is closely connected to fertility: each cycle involves the release of an egg, which travels to the uterus. If the egg is fertilized, pregnancy may develop; if it is not fertilized, a period occurs, marking the end of the cycle. Thus, pregnancy is a potential outcome of the menstrual cycle, and both are regulated by hormonal changes, including progesterone.</data>
      <data key="d12">MENSTRUAL CYCLE</data>
    </edge>
