      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is a federal agency of the United States. It operates within the U.S. federal government and is responsible for protecting public health by regulating various products. Notably, the FDA may approve new treatments after they have undergone clinical trials, ensuring that medical products meet safety and effectiveness standards before they are made available to the public. As a U.S. federal agency, it plays a key role in the nation's healthcare and regulatory systems.</data>
      <data key="d12">UNITED STATES</data>
    </edge>
